---
import ContentPage from '../layouts/ContentPage.astro';
import Secret from '../components/Secret.astro';
import { socials } from '../data/sections';
---

<ContentPage title="About Me" description="Daniel Beyer: full-stack engineer and game developer with a B.S. in Computer Science from Illinois State University.">
	<div class="prose">
		<p>
			Hey, I’m Daniel Beyer, a full-stack engineer and game developer with a B.S. in Computer Science and a minor in
			Mathematics from Illinois State University.
		</p>
		<p>
			I started programming in a high school game design class, modding a Unity game. After graduation, I taught myself
			Python, testing my, albeit tiny, skills by building a chess game, and started a blog to keep a record of what I was
			up to.
		</p>
		<p>
			Whether it’s a machine learning model, a video game, or a website, I like understanding the minute details behind
			what I build, even in our new era of vibe coding and convenience. Of course, in a world of shortening deadlines and
			growing scopes, I understand how to compromise my curiosity with efficiency where necessary.
		</p>
		<p>
			These days, I build web applications professionally and still make games when I can. Away from the <Secret id="about">keyboard</Secret>, I
			read, run, cook, draw, and, naturally, play video games.
		</p>
		<p>
			I’m looking for a software engineering role where I can keep learning and building things that people use, whether
			it be for professional, necessary, or leisurely applications.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div class="cta card">
		<p>Find me elsewhere</p>
		<ul class="jump-nav">
			{
				socials.map((s) => (
					<li>
						<a href={s.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
							{s.label}
						</a>
					</li>
				))
			}
		</ul>
	</div>
</ContentPage>
